    "created_at": "2016-08-05T05:42:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-05T05:42:02Z",
    "body": "Per http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4358 it appears Firefox, Chrome, and Edge all follow the spec here and have [OverrideBuildins] for form but not form.elements. (I assume Safari too, but while traveling I don't have my Mac.) Given that this is an old and icky API, I don't see a lot of value in changing this. Is there interest from Chrome in experimenting with being the first to change it? Otherwise I am inclined to close.\n\nIf it would help, we could add an example explicitly showing the inconsistency to the spec...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
